  "description": "We have a mature bay tree (Laurus nobilis) in our back garden area. Over the years it has developed an extensive shallow root system that is causing displacement of the garden paving and creating uneven surfaces within a small, constrained rear garden. \r\rThe tree is located in close proximity to a shared boundary wall with No 30 and continued root growth presents a risk of further structural impact to the hard landscaping and surrounding structures affecting our neighbours. \r\rRepair of the affected paving would require significant disturbance of the tree?s roots and is therefore unlikely to provide a sustainable long-term solution. \r\rThe proposal is therefore to remove the tree and replace it with a more suitable small ornamental species such as a single stemmed Prunus serrulata, together with a wider replanting scheme incorporating pollinator-friendly plants including lavender, salvia, echinacea and verbena. The proposal aims to maintain canopy cover through replacement planting while delivering an enhancement of the site?s biodiversity by introducing pollinator supporting planting.",
